<title>USA: USDA 7-State and U.S. Cattle on Feed.</title>
<headline>USDA 7-State and U.S. Cattle on Feed.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA cattle on feed,</p>
<p>1,000-plus head feedlots (data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    7 MAJOR STATES --  Pct----1997-----1996     1995</p>
<p> On Feed June 1	  113   8,226    7,253    8,182</p>
<p>During May:</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	 126   1,640    1,300    1,673</p>
<p> -Marketed		 104   1,818    1,747    1,667</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance  138	80	 58	 57</p>
<p> On Feed May 1	   109   8,484    7,758    8,233</p>
<p>The seven major states are Arizona, California, Colorado, Iowa,</p>
<p>Kansas, Nebraska and Texas.</p>
<p>USDA cattle on feed in the United States (1,000-plus head</p>
<p>feedlots, data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    U.S. TOTAL --	Pct----1997-----1996</p>
<p> On Feed June 1	  112   9,610    8,601</p>
<p>During May:</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	 122   1,892    1,557</p>
<p> -Marketed		 102   2,091    2,045</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance  139     117	 84</p>
<p> On Feed May 1	   108   9,926    9,173</p>
<p>The USDA said the year-to-year relationship between fed cattle marketed and commercial slaughter continued to be affected by the decrease in cattle imported from Canada that are going directly to slaughter.</p>
</text>
